    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside core, with **Corbin Carroll** leading the charge as our premier play (87.14). His matchup against Lorenzen is statistically optimal, pairing an elite 8-spot order rank with significant park and platoon advantages. **James Wood** (78.42) follows closely as a primary driver; he is locked into the leadoff spot against Young, and his 0.380 xwOBA profile suggests he is primed to exploit this matchup. We are also leaning heavily into the power-potential of **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21); the latter specifically benefits from a favorable wind projection that provides a crucial boost to his power profile, pushing his efficiency well into our \"Strong\" tier.\n\nStrategic attention turns to **Brice Turang** (68.77) and **Mickey Moniak** (73.28), both of whom are start-worthy due to secondary category utility. **Brice Turang** is particularly intriguing given the \"Slow SP Delivery\" metric, which highlights a high stolen base probability, a priority category for this team. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a 14% boost via park effects and platoon dynamics, effectively negating the moderate threat posed by Soroka. While **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing** provide solid production, the optimizer remains slightly more cautious about their bottom-of-the-order positioning.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros** (45.40), who sat on the bubble of our starting rotation. Ultimately, **Kyle Karros** was bypassed because his projected efficiency failed to surpass our depth at corner infield, particularly with **Austin Riley** (65.82) and **Josh Naylor** (71.66) providing more reliable floor outcomes. We continue to monitor the status of **Jose Caballero** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our late-game substitution flexibility. Keep a close watch on **Brice Turang**, as the forecasted wind-in conditions pose the only notable risk to his power output despite his favorable stolen base projections.",
